{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PmtcyjtijhupUzCHhnFgfJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tSCOPE: payload 14/32 = first piece of the .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py diff. audit_emit.py becomes a facade (imports, _KNOWN_ACTIONS literal, iter_events, emit_credential_rotation_due) that binds 33 template modules under .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/ into its own namespace via _audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:install(). Limit: the base audit_emit.py is not in the read-only tree and this payload shows only the start of its diff. Equivalence was checked against the removed text visible here plus counts and spot checks, not byte-for-byte against the whole old file. Tests could not be run.\n2\t\n3\tDECLARED CONDITIONS TOUCHED BY THIS PAYLOAD\n4\t- Condition 7 (thin entry points over _lib modules; lookups stay on the facade): TRUE for this file. audit_emit.py:413-452 installs the parts. install() rebuilds each function with FunctionType(code, facade_globals, ...), so name lookups and test patch points (for example audit_emit._log_path) still resolve on the facade.\n5\t- Condition 5 (kernel coverage of the split packages): TRUE for this package. check_arbitration_kernel.py:312 lists .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*.\n6\t\n7\tCHECKS PERFORMED (no defect found)\n8\t- Action list: _KNOWN_ACTIONS at audit_emit.py:45-377 has 331 unique entries, matching the old count recorded in the removed comments (327->330 plus session_memory_delta_observed). No installed part overrides it; only actions.py exports that name, and it is not installed.\n9\t- Pass-through list: _EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH (federation_schemas.py:214-399) matches the old region visible in the diff, including the \"MOVED/REMOVED from passthrough\" notes. Actions with their own field filter (invisible_unicode_blocked, model_refusal_observed, statusline_sidecar_write, mcp_injection_finding, admin_key_lifecycle_event, bash_canonical_bypass_invoked, spawn_confidence_adv