h tuple prevents.** At `generic_dispatch_05.py:359-360` the comment says every handler stays bound to the front module so it can be patched at run time. But `_dispatch_generic` loops over `_GENERIC_DISPATCH_HANDLERS`, a tuple built once at `audit_emit.py:464-470`. Patching `audit_emit._apply_generic_group_0N` therefore has no effect on dispatch. Fix: have `_dispatch_generic` look each handler up by name at call time, or reword the comment.\n2. **P2, already raised in the rc review:** stand-ins kept for source-scanning checks. These are the duplicate `iter_events` definitions (`audit_emit.py:21`, `:382`, `:457-461`) and the three identical branches in `emit_generic` (`:473-480`). Behaviour is the same, but checks like `check-audit-read-api-stable.py` now inspect stand-ins instead of the real code.\n3. **P2, already raised in the rc review:** `_audit_emit_parts/actions.py`, `actions_core.py` and `actions_extended.py` hold a second, never-installed copy of the action list that can drift silently from the live list.\n4. **P2, already raised in the rc review:** the module docstring and its design rules were removed and appear nowhere in the front module.\n5. **Related, already in the rc notes:** the `writer.py` fallback references `line` before it is set (codex-p03). Also, the new front module depends on 33 more files at import time, so a partial install now has more ways to break the import. That is the class of the annexed `check_canonical_edit.py:624` P1 (codex-p17/p22), which treats an import failure as an integrity failure. Nothing here is new.\n\n**Limits of this review**\n- `scripts/upgrade.sh` was withheld from the copy, so I checked install delivery only through `install.sh:1522-1547` and `_framework_manifest_set.sh:95-107`. The package is not excluded there.\n- I checked for names defined in more than one part on a sample of about 50 names, not on every name in every `__all__`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usa