r, the GC sweep, should_emit_context_pressure with O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW and a random temp name, clear_context_pressure_marker); tokens_boot.py:190-227; confidence.py:18-63; pair_rail.py:165-182; operations.py; orchestration.py:288-497; federation_persona.py:17-411.\n- Name resolution: every name removed in this payload is defined once in an installed part (grep of the definitions). The 33 installed parts are all the part files except actions/actions_core/actions_extended. writer.py holds _write_event, _breadcrumb and _log_path. adapters.py:314 holds _ATLAS_REGISTRY. federation_schemas.py:214 holds _EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH.\n- Binding and patch points: install() (_audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:20-48) rebuilds every function with FunctionType(code, facade_globals, ...), so patching audit_emit._write_event or _log_path still takes effect. _try_rate_admit's globals() resolves to the front module. Mutable values are deep-copied on each import or reload. The locks cannot be deep-copied and are not exported by any part; the front module creates them at audit_emit.py:483-484, before any call. iter_events delegates to the replay implementation bound to the front module (audit_emit.py:457-461). Only replay exports iter_events, and no part exports emit_generic or emit_credential_rotation_due, so the front module's own definitions win.\n- Dispatch and fail direction: _dispatch_generic (generic_dispatch_05.py:361-377) drops unknown actions with a breadcrumb. A handler that returns None drops the malformed event without writing, True writes the cleaned event, and the default writes only {\"action\": action}. The tool_call_lifecycle_recorded and settings_tamper_detected branches are in generic_dispatch_04.py:62 and :159. The old code had no top-level try either, so there is no fail-open/fail-closed inversion.\n- Python 3.9 and standard library only: typing names the front module no longer imports appear only in annotations kept as strings by \"from __future__ import annotations\". There is no cast, TypeVar, NamedTuple or get_type_hints. Deep-copying re.Pattern is supported from 3.7. SimpleNamespace and the FunctionType call work on 3.9.\n- Consumers that load the file by path: verify-atlas-binding.py:107, check_atlas_fpr.py:83 and tier_policy_cli/apply.py:361-366 load audit_emit.py with spec_from_file_location. Module-level install() still populates _ATLAS_REGISTRY and _KNOWN_ACTIONS, and the front module adds the hooks directory to sys.path itself (audit_emit.py:15-17). check-audit-action-name-convention.py and check-audit-registry-coverage.py still find the _KNOWN_ACTIONS literal in the front module.\n- Adopter delivery: install.sh:1522-1547 copies every _lib entry, and _framework_manifest_set.sh:95-107 does not exclude _audit_emit_parts.\n- Writes: the context-pressure marker and shard-counter writes are the old code, including the declared rc.1 condition-28 limits on counter reads.\n\nP0: none.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none at P1.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n1. P2 (new) - .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/generic_dispatch_05.py:359-368 with .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:464-470. The comment says every handler stays bound to the front module so it can be patched at run time. But _dispatch_generic loops over _GENERIC_DISPATCH_HANDLERS, a tuple captured once at import, so patching audit_emit._apply_generic_group_0N does not change dispatch. Failure scenario: a test or a maintainer's hotfix patches a group handler and the original keeps running without notice. Minimal fix: look the handlers up by name at call time (for example a tuple of names resolved through globals()), or correct the comment.\n2. P2 (already raised in the rc review, rc1-14 item 2) - audit_emit.py:21, :382-383, :455-461, :473-480. Duplicate iter_events definitions, the replay template imported under the name _streaming, and three identical emit_generic branches, kept for source-scanning checks. Same behaviour, but those checks inspect stand-ins. Fix: add a comment stating the purpose, or have the checks follow the install list.\n3. P2 (already raised, rc1-14 item 1 and rc1-27 item 7) - _audit_emit_parts/actions.py, actions_core.py, actions_extended.py: a second, never-installed copy of _KNOWN_ACTIONS that can drift from the live literal. Fix: delete it, or have a check assert the two sets are equal.\n4. P2 (already raised, rc1-14 item 3) - audit_emit.py:1: the module docstring and its design rules were removed.\n5. Related, already in the rc lane notes (codex-p03, codex-p17/p22): the writer.py fallback references the variable line before it is set. The front module's import now also depends on 33 more files, which widens the partial-install class of the annexed check_canonical_edit.py:624 P1 (an ImportError treated as an integrity failure). Nothing new here.","decision":"GO","sentence":"This payload only finishes moving audit_emit.py into _lib/_audit_emit_parts: the moved text is unchanged, every name resolves once and is looked up through the facade's namespace, the locks and the spool-writer hookup are kept, the code stays Python 3.9 standard-library only, conditions 5, 7 and 8 hold, and I found no P0 or new P1, only P2 follow-ups."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2680,"cache_read_input_tokens":202845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2680},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"718cdb07-6dd0-4fda-8536-67e04c6aa837","uuid":"fa942e9c-87e5-4956-8bea-e72bf93b0651","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:07:56.306Z","request_id":"req_011Ch78Yt7JqKdTcKpSbjkNf","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014fFDJEg6ZCmsZkoHUXAwvm":{"report":"SCOPE: payload 17/34, the end of the .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py diff. About 13,000 lines ar