inal keeps running without notice. Minimal fix: look the handlers up by name at call time (for example a tuple of names resolved through globals()), or correct the comment.\n2. P2 (already raised in the rc review, rc1-14 item 2) - audit_emit.py:21, :382-383, :455-461, :473-480. Duplicate iter_events definitions, the replay template imported under the name _streaming, and three identical emit_generic branches, kept for source-scanning checks. Same behaviour, but those checks inspect stand-ins. Fix: add a comment stating the purpose, or have the checks follow the install list.\n3. P2 (already raised, rc1-14 item 1 and rc1-27 item 7) - _audit_emit_parts/actions.py, actions_core.py, actions_extended.py: a second, never-installed copy of _KNOWN_ACTIONS that can drift from the live literal. Fix: delete it, or have a check assert the two sets are equal.\n4. P2 (already raised, rc1-14 item 3) - audit_emit.py:1: the module docstring and its design rules were removed.\n5. Related, already in the rc lane notes (codex-p03, codex-p17/p22): the writer.py fallback references the variable line before it is set. The front module's import now also depends on 33 more files, which widens the partial-install class of the annexed check_canonical_edit.py:624 P1 (an ImportError treated as an integrity failure). Nothing new here.","decision":"GO","sentence":"This payload only finishes moving audit_emit.py into _lib/_audit_emit_parts: the moved text is unchanged, every name resolves once and is looked up through the facade's namespace, the locks and the spool-writer hookup are kept, the code stays Python 3.9 standard-library only, conditions 5, 7 and 8 hold, and I found no P0 or new P1, only P2 follow-ups."},"ttft_ms":11502,"type":"result","duration_ms":400545,"uuid":"8e19359b-c593-4271-b4f0-7a35c60a438e","ttft_stream_ms":5894,"time_to_request_ms":198,"first_content_frame_ms":5895,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":68,"out